Hello!  I've been putting some ideas into #nethack's ideas pool recently, 
and decided to implement two of the ideas that caught my attention.

The first of these allows you to hit monsters with scrolls and possibly 
invoke some of the scroll's magic, e.g. hitting monsters with a scroll of 
fire will burn them (effective against paper golems!).

The second (but first chronologically) of these grants gelatinous cubes 
(and water elementals) a new engulfing attack which suffocates the target, 
as befits the cube's D&D behaviour (and will hopefully return to it the 
fearsome position it deserves!).

The two patches are available in Pasi's patch database:
Scrolls: http://bilious.homelinux.org/?236
Attack:  http://bilious.homelinux.org/?234

I'm not in a position where I can compile these for Windows platforms, but 
someone else is welcome to do this if they enjoy the patches.

Have fun with these!

